# migration tooling artifacts
_tools/node_modules/
_tools/*-log.txt
# Generated working page (~550KB of inlined thumbnails). Regenerate with
# build-ls-callsheet.js; GitHub Pages would otherwise serve it publicly.
_tools/ls-callsheet.html
# .claude/ is committed on purpose: the pricing-strategy skill is a durable
# project asset, not a local scratch file. Note the repo is public, so keep
# secrets out of it -- the same rule CLAUDE.md states.

# _tools/scraped/ is committed on purpose: it is the raw archival copy of the
# live Weebly pages, the only source if a transform fix is ever needed after
# Weebly shuts down.

# Generated image bundles for uploading elsewhere (see _tools/export-ls-images.js).
# These are copies of art already in the repo; no reason to version them twice.
_export/

# Generator 2.0 redemption codes and the PDFs built from them. These are LIVE
# LemonSqueezy discount codes and this repo is public (and .nojekyll is on, so
# _-prefixed paths are served verbatim). make_pdfs.py reads the codes from the
# untracked JSON and refuses to run without it. The built PDFs are delivered
# through the LemonSqueezy product download, never from this repo.
_content/redemption-docs/redemption-codes.json
_content/redemption-docs/*.pdf
